{"id": "nexstreet-district-contracts", "title": "A district's former director runs the company that gets most of its budget", "seconds": 130.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.138, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "bac270b9d7ea81fa", "words": 421, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "A director ran the Lower Polk Community Benefit District until 2019.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.64, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "executive director to Nov 8, 2019"}, {"art": "van", "name": "NexStreet - Cleaning and Sanitation", "sub": "chief executive, per Lower Polk"}], "kicker": "The former director"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.52, 0.74, 0.86, 1.11, 1.3, 1.71, 2.05, 2.41, 2.65, 2.92]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Its tax returns now name him chief executive of its cleaning company, NexStreet.", "t0": 3.76, "t1": 7.4, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "Lower Polk Community Benefit District", "sub": "executive director to Nov 8, 2019"}, {"art": "van", "name": "NexStreet - Cleaning and Sanitation", "sub": "chief executive, per Lower Polk"}], "kicker": "The former director"}, "emph": ["NexStreet"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.43, 0.8, 1.0, 1.2, 1.31, 1.54, 2.05, 2.16, 2.29, 2.62, 3.11]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "In the year to June 2025, how much did the district pay NexStreet?", "t0": 7.52, "t1": 11.8, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Lower Polk paid NexStreet", "sub": "year to June 30, 2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.28, 0.51, 0.65, 0.91, 1.18, 2.1, 2.32, 2.55, 2.67, 2.8, 3.13, 3.37]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0].what", "established[1]"], "text": "920,369 dollars.", "t0": 11.8, "t1": 14.28, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$920,369", "label": "paid to NexStreet by Lower Polk", "sub": "60.6% of everything it spent"}, "emph": ["920,369"], "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.49, 0.77, 1.16, 1.39, 1.64, 2.12]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 14.8, "t1": 16.34, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.28, 0.37, 0.91, 1.09, 1.16]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Benefit districts clean streets and run ambassador patrols.", "t0": 16.46, "t1": 18.98, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City of San Francisco", "sub": "collects the assessment"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Lower Polk district", "sub": "cleans and patrols"}, {"art": "van", "name": "NexStreet", "sub": "the vendor"}], "kicker": "How a benefit district is paid"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.69, 0.94, 1.25, 1.37, 1.56, 2.03]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "Property owners pay an extra assessment, and the City passes it on.", "t0": 19.1, "t1": 22.06, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "City of San Francisco", "sub": "collects the assessment"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Lower Polk district", "sub": "cleans and patrols"}, {"art": "van", "name": "NexStreet", "sub": "the vendor"}], "kicker": "How a benefit district is paid"}, "emph": ["passes it on"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.62, 0.78, 0.89, 1.12, 1.66, 1.83, 1.95, 2.22, 2.57, 2.68]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "That one payment is 60.6 percent of everything the district spent.", "t0": 22.28, "t1": 25.72, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paid to NexStreet, year to June 2025", "$920,369"], "b": ["all Lower Polk spending", "$1,517,549"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["60.6 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.37, 0.8, 1.02, 1.39, 1.65, 1.87, 2.22, 2.32, 2.68, 2.78, 3.11]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Its own staff fell from 6 to 2.", "t0": 25.84, "t1": 27.44, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paid to NexStreet, year to June 2025", "$920,369"], "b": ["all Lower Polk spending", "$1,517,549"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.35, 0.65, 0.84, 0.99, 1.2, 1.3]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "defense[0]"], "text": "The district disclosed it on its return: former executive director, now chief executive of the vendor.", "t0": 27.56, "t1": 32.54, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Former ED; now CEO of vendor"}, "emph": ["now chief executive"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.45, 0.87, 0.97, 1.09, 1.22, 2.03, 2.36, 2.8, 3.52, 3.74, 3.99, 4.48, 4.56, 4.66]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[9]", "established[11]"], "text": "The state’s company filings agree: he signed its June 2021 registration as chief executive.", "t0": 32.66, "t1": 37.5, "shot": "b6b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Secretary of State 4756745", "kicker": "The state’s company record", "sub": "signed as chief executive, June 2021 registration: the former director"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.41, 0.75, 1.15, 1.79, 1.93, 2.21, 2.37, 2.63, 2.9, 3.37, 3.96, 4.09, 4.34]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Most of a public district’s budget, to its former boss’s firm?", "t0": 37.62, "t1": 40.85, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The price and the choice", "kicker": "Why it matters", "sub": "need independent proof"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.34, 0.4, 0.69, 1.07, 1.56, 1.72, 1.87, 2.17, 2.54]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Then the price and the choice need independent proof.", "t0": 40.85, "t1": 43.24, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "The price and the choice", "kicker": "Why it matters", "sub": "need independent proof"}, "emph": ["independent proof"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.36, 0.69, 0.79, 0.9, 1.24, 1.5, 2.07]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "He resigned on November 8, 2019.", "t0": 43.46, "t1": 45.52, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-11-08", "to": "2022-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "Director resigns", "toLab": "$267,390 to NexStreet", "kicker": "Out, then in"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.54, 0.64, 1.05, 1.26, 1.56]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "By June 2022, the district had paid NexStreet 267,390 dollars.", "t0": 45.64, "t1": 51.0, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-11-08", "to": "2022-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "Director resigns", "toLab": "$267,390 to NexStreet", "kicker": "Out, then in"}, "emph": ["267,390"], "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.42, 0.67, 1.36, 1.5, 1.83, 1.95, 2.2, 2.64, 2.88, 3.16, 3.8, 4.19, 4.42, 4.71, 4.95]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "The next year, 237,797.", "t0": 51.12, "t1": 54.6, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2019-11-08", "to": "2022-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "Director resigns", "toLab": "$267,390 to NexStreet", "kicker": "Out, then in"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.37, 0.81, 1.02, 1.25, 1.81, 2.23, 2.56, 2.84]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "That’s the classic revolving-door risk. The seller knows the budget, the board and the contract terms.", "t0": 54.72, "t1": 59.67, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the seller knows the budget, the board and the contract terms"}, "emph": ["revolving-door"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.3, 0.69, 1.37, 1.92, 2.06, 2.35, 2.56, 2.66, 3.18, 3.34, 3.74, 4.02, 4.13, 4.57]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].what", "established[4]"], "text": "Where had he gone? To run another district, SOMA West.", "t0": 59.89, "t1": 63.09, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "SOMA West Community Benefit District", "kicker": "His next job", "sub": "executive director, 40 hours a week", "chip": "$247,612 in FY2025"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.34, 0.44, 1.28, 1.44, 1.61, 1.9, 2.46, 2.83]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "suspicious[2].what", "established[4]"], "text": "In 2025 it paid him 247,612 dollars.", "t0": 63.21, "t1": 67.34, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "SOMA West Community Benefit District", "kicker": "His next job", "sub": "executive director, 40 hours a week", "chip": "$247,612 in FY2025"}, "emph": ["247,612"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.42, 1.03, 1.14, 1.34, 1.45, 1.66, 1.92, 2.54, 2.96, 3.2, 3.44, 3.73]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[5]"], "text": "A City official said a third district hired him as director in 2022.", "t0": 67.46, "t1": 70.76, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Ocean Avenue Association", "kicker": "A third district", "sub": "hired him in 2022, a City official said"}, "emph": ["third district"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.73, 0.89, 0.97, 1.2, 1.54, 1.77, 1.88, 2.0, 2.42, 2.51, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[5]"], "text": "The Ocean Avenue Association. He still held the SOMA West job.", "t0": 70.88, "t1": 74.15, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Ocean Avenue Association", "kicker": "A third district", "sub": "hired him in 2022, a City official said"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.41, 0.69, 1.77, 1.93, 2.17, 2.36, 2.46, 2.74, 2.98]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[6]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Ocean Avenue’s returns don’t name him. They report an unnamed local management company.", "t0": 74.27, "t1": 78.17, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "engaged the services of a local management company"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.66, 1.07, 1.28, 1.49, 1.98, 2.15, 2.46, 2.56, 2.89, 3.15, 3.52]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[6]", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "Of all these roles, only Lower Polk’s return discloses any.", "t0": 78.29, "t1": 81.18, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "engaged the services of a local management company"}, "emph": ["only Lower Polk"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.29, 0.49, 1.02, 1.28, 1.54, 1.8, 2.16, 2.66]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "established[7]"], "text": "NexStreet is paid by two more City-funded groups.", "t0": 81.4, "t1": 83.67, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to NexStreet, by City-funded groups", "rows": [["Lower Polk CBD, FY2025", "920369"], ["Mid Market Foundation, 2024", "718793"], ["Japantown CBD, FY2025", "235968"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.55, 0.77, 0.92, 1.16, 1.38, 1.92]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "established[7]"], "text": "Mid Market Foundation, 718,793 dollars in 2024.", "t0": 83.79, "t1": 88.56, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to NexStreet, by City-funded groups", "rows": [["Lower Polk CBD, FY2025", "920369"], ["Mid Market Foundation, 2024", "718793"], ["Japantown CBD, FY2025", "235968"]]}, "emph": ["718,793"], "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.52, 1.28, 1.57, 1.8, 2.16, 2.57, 2.85, 3.1, 3.57, 3.91, 3.99, 4.26]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what", "established[7]"], "text": "And Japantown’s district, 235,968.", "t0": 88.68, "t1": 92.37, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Paid to NexStreet, by City-funded groups", "rows": [["Lower Polk CBD, FY2025", "920369"], ["Mid Market Foundation, 2024", "718793"], ["Japantown CBD, FY2025", "235968"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.77, 1.42, 1.61, 1.85, 2.39, 2.78, 2.97, 3.19]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[10]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "All three print the same Oakland address beside it. It is one company at all three.", "t0": 92.49, "t1": 96.39, "shot": "b13a", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "8055 Collins Dr, Oakland, CA 94621"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.47, 0.67, 0.78, 1.07, 1.33, 1.67, 2.02, 2.46, 2.62, 2.75, 2.93, 3.29, 3.38, 3.56]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[14]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "The City registry even lists a NexStreet account at Lower Polk’s own address, from 2023.", "t0": 96.51, "t1": 101.04, "shot": "b13b", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "1170 Sutter Street", "kicker": "The City’s business registry", "sub": "a NexStreet account from April 2023, at Lower Polk’s registered address"}, "emph": ["Lower Polk’s own address"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 0.86, 1.1, 1.32, 1.41, 1.79, 2.1, 2.21, 2.46, 2.74, 2.88, 3.52, 3.7, 3.97]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "innocent[1]"], "text": "Japantown switched to it from another firm, Block by Block. Neither group reports any insider tie.", "t0": 101.16, "t1": 106.12, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Japantown’s cleaner, FY2023", "Block by Block"], "b": ["from FY2024", "NexStreet"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["Block by Block"], "wt": [0.0, 0.61, 0.89, 1.04, 1.13, 1.28, 1.58, 1.99, 2.26, 2.4, 3.18, 3.46, 3.69, 4.02, 4.2, 4.62]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["defense[0]", "story[3]"], "text": "Lower Polk’s answer, on its return: the vendor was chosen by an open, public, objective bidding process.", "t0": 106.24, "t1": 111.58, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Vendor selection was based on an open, public, objective RFP process ensuring no excess benefit."}, "emph": ["open, public"], "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.54, 0.93, 1.12, 1.25, 2.12, 2.25, 2.52, 2.65, 3.0, 3.18, 3.32, 3.72, 4.12, 4.61, 4.85]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "That bidding record hasn’t been seen. And nothing shows the work wasn’t done, or was overpriced.", "t0": 111.8, "t1": 116.67, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["The RFP: who bid, how bids were scored, who voted", "That NexStreet’s work was not done or was overpriced"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.44, 0.73, 0.99, 1.16, 1.89, 2.11, 2.4, 2.69, 2.8, 3.02, 3.29, 3.79, 4.01, 4.25]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]"], "text": "What would settle it? Lower Polk’s bids, scoring and board votes. And SOMA West’s conflict-of-interest disclosures.", "t0": 116.79, "t1": 122.56, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Lower Polk: the RFP, the bids, the scoring and the board votes"}, {"who": "", "what": "SOMA West: its director’s conflict-of-interest disclosures"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.31, 0.58, 1.13, 1.39, 1.67, 2.16, 2.53, 2.64, 2.89, 3.52, 3.77, 4.08, 4.39, 5.18]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[1]"], "text": "No authority has ruled on this. No statement from the former director or NexStreet was found.", "t0": 122.68, "t1": 127.07, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.69, 0.83, 1.06, 1.18, 1.87, 2.06, 2.41, 2.54, 2.65, 2.94, 3.37, 3.49, 3.9, 4.03]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.19, "t1": 129.25, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.33, 0.44, 0.51, 1.14, 1.34, 1.44]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Lead 1 · 60.6% of spending", "lead2": "Lead 2 · the revolving door", "lead3": "Lead 3 · three districts", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the same vendor", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "person"}